 "known_issues": [
  "Synthetic: generated by CAMBER's own model of a VAV system, not measured. It shows what the rules see, not how a real system behaves; never cite it as evidence about real buildings.",
  "The resets take three trim-and-respond cycles per trended hour (a 20-minute step; G36's default is 2 minutes) and the trend keeps the hour's last cycle, so reset_effectiveness reconstructs them from one request count per hour: closely, not exactly. A real controller cycles every few minutes; on an hourly trend of one, the rule's reconstruction is coarser still.",
  "Generator version 3 (0.108, #226): the zones' loads rise and fall together, both resets hold their start value with the fan off, and a tier-1 request holds until the loop or the damper falls below 85 %, so the healthy air handler's zones are comfortable and its boxes track their airflow setpoint. In version 2 a lone perimeter zone sat 3-5 F warm for hours under a correct reset that ignores two requests, and unmet_setpoint_hours and airflow_tracking flagged the healthy boxes.",
  "The fleet rules (the rogue-zone and cohort-starvation censuses, cohort_airflow, cohort_space_temp, zones_heat_cool_census) report one finding for the whole facility, on <fleet>: camber datasets score cannot score them, and the census rules group the boxes under their air handler only through a served-by topology (the run template declares one).",
  "Each box trends its active airflow setpoint (ZN{n}_FLOW_SP, airflow_sp) and its minimum (ZN{n}_FLOW_MIN, airflow_min_sp) apart, and its heating and cooling loops (zone_heat_loop, zone_cool_loop) since generator version 2 (0.106). The cooling loop is the zone's cooling demand as a share of its cooling maximum: the box holds its minimum airflow below about 30 %, a simplification of G36's sequence, and the loop over 95 % is the same tier-1 SAT request the air handler's SAT_REQ counts.",
  "The fighting boxes of the heat_cool air handler report a heating loop at half their reheat valve (the dual-maximum valve range) together with a cooling loop that includes the reheat they add; a real controller with overlapping setpoints would show the two loops fighting the same way, though not with these exact values."
